// Application resources of the launcher.
//
// The icon is shared by every executable of the repository and lives in the
// docs directory. The resource compiler resolves this relative path through its
// search path, which contains the directory of this file (CMake passes the
// include directories of the target to the resource compiler).
//
// IDI_ICON1 is the icon group of the launcher executable, and Windows shows the
// first group of the resource directory order for a file, so this group is what
// Explorer shows for the extracted program.
//
// A packed launcher carries a second icon group as well: the packer appends the
// icon of the packaged application below a resource name which the resource
// directory orders before this one (see src/core/ApplicationIcon.cpp), so
// Explorer shows the icon of the packaged application for the extracted
// program while this group stays the icon of the launcher.
IDI_ICON1 ICON DISCARDABLE "../docs/icon.ico"

// The two sandbox injection modules the launcher releases into the cache
// directory of the sandbox at every start, declared as RCDATA resources of
// this executable. The identifiers are declared in the header of the launcher
// and used by the code which reads them back, and the statements themselves
// live in a file which CMake generates at configure time, because the modules
// are build products of this build tree (see launcher/EmbeddedResourceIds.h,
// cmake/LauncherResources.rc.in and launcher/CMakeLists.txt).
//
// The packer writes two more resources into the payload of the launcher when it
// packs an archive: the run configuration (IDR_APPBOX_LAUNCHER_CONFIG) and, when
// the session sets one, the startup image (IDR_APPBOX_STARTUP_IMAGE), both as
// RCDATA (see src/core/LauncherResources.cpp). Neither is declared here: a bare
// launcher carries no such resource, so a session without an image needs no
// resource at all. Their identifiers live in launcher/EmbeddedResourceIds.h, so
// the packer which writes them and the launcher which reads them back agree on
// the numbers.
#include "EmbeddedResourceIds.h"
#include "LauncherResources.generated.rc"
